What was read in ble.sh (lib/core-complete.sh, the auto-complete section) and
kept as behaviour, written again here in Rust and shell:

  * A suggestion is made only when the cursor is at the end of a non-empty
    line, and never for a command that is exactly what was typed.
  * The keys that take it: Right and End and Ctrl-E take all of it; Alt-F and
    Ctrl-Right take one word; Alt-Right takes a whitespace-delimited word and
    the blanks around it (ble.sh's insert-word, whose rule is "blanks, then
    the non-blanks, then blanks").
  * Any other key withdraws the suggestion and is then handled as usual.
  * The history is the source, the most recent command with the prefix first
    (the order inkling started from; it has since put its own on it).

No source text of ble.sh is in this repository, so none of its licence's
